ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "4.3", text = "Radials that know which character they belong to, a cleaner Radial Menu page, an official FlareUI Edit Mode layout, a round minimap and two action bar tweaks.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Radial Menu: each radial has its own |cffffffffAvailable to|r (all characters, all Alliance or Horde characters, all characters of a class, or only this character) and its own |cffffffffKey|r, shared by every character that gets it. Your characters pick up their radials at login, so a Druid radial stays on your Druids. Two radials can share a key: on a character that gets both, the narrower one wins. Tick |cffffffffOnly this character|r to give one character its own key.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffCopy|r a radial (handy for a Horde or class version), and |cffffffffCreate macro|r right next to its key.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffStyle|r, Square (the default) or Round, Forever's own round minimap, thanks to parchinskiy. Needs a reload.\n• The |cffffffffFlareUI Edit Mode layout|r: copy its code from the bottom of the About page (or the new page in the setup tour) and import it in Edit Mode to set your screen up like ours.\n• Action Bars, Tweaks: |cffffffffSteady attack highlight|r (on): Attack, Auto Shot and Shoot stay lit in red while they're on, instead of blinking.\n• Action Bars, Tweaks: |cffffffffGryphons behind bars|r (off): the art at each end of the main bar sits behind your bars instead of over them.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Radial Menu page: one Radials tab with your radials on the right, what opens on this character below them, and a bigger editor with a two-column Catalog. The Keybinds tab is gone: your keys were moved onto your radials and every character keeps the keys it had.\n• Radial Menu now sits below Quality of Life in the settings list.\n• Party frames: new default places for Forever Style and FlareUI Style (frames you already moved stay where they are).\n• Quest Tracker: an empty tracker says why, instead of looking minimized.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action bar 1: the page arrows no longer hide under the left gryphon.\n• Pet bar with Show button art: the frames no longer hang over each other." },
    { version = "4.2", text = "Stack counts get their own font, chat windows can be made click-through from the tab menu, and every aura frame now follows one shared set of rules, which fixes several aura bugs.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Buffs & Debuffs and Unit Frames: |cffffffffAura stacks|r font on the Fonts tab, with face, size, outline and shadow for stack counts, separate from the timers. It starts as a copy of your timer font, so nothing changes until you edit it. On unit frames its size can be |cffffffffAuto|r (the default), sized to the icon.\n• Chat: |cffffffffMake Uninteractable|r in the chat tab's right-click menu, Blizzard's own option. Links in that window stop reacting and it can't be resized. Docked windows switch together. Right-click the tab again to undo it.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit Frames, Aura timers font: its Size now works. |cffffffffAuto|r (the default) keeps sizing the timer to the icon.\n• Party, raid and main tank frames: with dispel icons on, a debuff you can dispel shows only as its dispel icon, no longer a second time in the debuff row, like Blizzard's raid frames.\n• Boss frames pick their debuffs the same way as the target frame, no longer by party-frame rules.\n• The \"Restore your Edit Mode layout?\" prompt after switching characters now reloads your interface to finish the switch.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Target, focus and pet: |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r hid other players' debuffs on friendly units and on yourself. It now filters enemies only, like Blizzard's target frame.\n• Action bars could vanish in combat until the fight ended after restoring an Edit Mode layout from FlareUI's prompt.\n• A Lua error when opening Edit Mode in combat or in an instance with Buffs & Debuffs on.\n• Party and raid frames: the dispel highlight added a hidden slot each time you changed its look in Edit Mode.\n• Pet frame: Hide Buffs no longer hides timed buffs while the pet is far away, like target and focus." },
    { version = "4.1", text = "Your damage meter as a chat tab, a real Clear All for raid markers, and two fixes.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Damage Meter: |cffffffffMeter tab in the chat|r, off by default, thanks to Gregory Duhamel. A Meter tab joins your chat tabs and shows Blizzard's meter inside the chat window, at the chat's size. Click a chat tab to get the chat back, in combat too. A chat tab whose messages arrive while the meter covers them lights up. Find it in Settings > Damage Meter > Meter Tab, with:\n      - |cffffffffOpen the Meter tab|r: When clicked, In combat (back to the chat after the fight, the default), In group or At login.\n      - |cffffffffIgnore chat fade|r: the chat window stays up while the Meter tab is open.\n      - While the tab is on, the meter's own Visibility waits, and it doesn't show in the Gamepad UI.\n• Radial menu: |cffffffffClear All Markers|r removes every raid marker on players and enemies at once. Add it from the Markers category in the radial menu editor. New radials get it on their own.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Radial menu: the two old clear slices now say what they do: |cffffffffClear Target's Marker|r and |cffffffffClear World Markers|r (the flares on the ground). If your \"Clear All\" slice never removed the marks over heads, it was Clear World Markers: swap it for Clear All Markers.\n• Combat + Attackable Target (Fake Cooldown Manager, fading bars and Resource Bars): a dead target no longer counts, so clicking a corpse to loot it doesn't bring the bars back.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Player cast bar with Cinematic: it no longer stays hidden after a login or /reload." },
    { version = "4.0", text = "A lighter FlareUI: the same features, doing far less work behind the scenes. Plus separate buff and debuff sizes, a lighter Forever bar texture and macro cooldowns in the radial menu.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\n|cffffd100Performance|r\nFlareUI got a full performance pass. Nothing was removed or changed in how it looks or works; it just stops redoing work that hasn't changed. In our own testing, FlareUI's CPU use stayed under 0.2%.\n• Power bars: a power change was drawn twice in the same frame. Now once. Most noticeable for energy and rage.\n• Resource Bars: each power tick now only moves the bar and its number, and the Druid Mana bar ignores energy and rage ticks.\n• Quest tracker: it reads the quest log once per redraw instead of three times, no longer rebuilds the whole list every 2 seconds while you stand still, and skips text and fonts that haven't changed.\n• Fading bars: bars that have finished fading are no longer checked 20 times a second.\n• Proc glows: only warriors and paladins follow the target's health (for Execute and Hammer of Wrath).\n• Party frames: in a raid, the hidden party frames no longer re-lay out on every roster change or raid pet change, and hidden pet and target tiles wait until they show.\n• Threat meter: no work while it's hidden or faded out, and it reuses its lists instead of building new ones up to five times a second.\n• Unit frames: fewer updates per health and power tick on the player frame, the mana cost overlay and the quest icon.\n• New: |cffffffff/fui perf|r measures FlareUI with Blizzard's addon profiler. |cffffd100/fui perf start <name>|r records a scenario, |cffffd100/fui perf stop|r saves it and |cffffd100/fui perf report|r gives you text to paste in a bug report.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Every frame with auras: |cffffffffBuffs Size|r and |cffffffffDebuffs Size|r replace Aura Size, so each can have its own size. Both start at your old Aura Size. On party, raid and boss frames, dispel icons follow Debuffs Size.\n• Health Text: |cffffffffCurrent | Max|r on every unit, party, raid and boss frame, in every style, and on the Resource Bars health bar.\n• Bar textures: |cffffffffFlareUI Forever (Light)|r, the Forever texture as bright as FlareUI Flat. FlareUI Forever stays as it was, and stays the default.\n• Mana on Shapeshift: the druid mana strip now shows its number when Power Text is on.\n• Radial menu: a macro shows the cooldown, the usable state and the icon of the spell or item it would cast right now, following |cffffd100#showtooltip|r and conditions like |cffffd100[mod:shift]|r. In the radial menu editor, macros show that spell's or item's tooltip.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Target of target and target of focus always show the first name only, whatever Full Player Names is set to.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Party frames: pets now fade when out of range, like the members." },
    { version = "3.0.9", text = "Quests that accept and turn themselves in, swing timers only when you're swinging, and FlareUI in Brazilian Portuguese.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffAuto accept quests|r and |cffffffffAuto turn-in quests|r, both off by default. Hold Shift to stop them for a moment. Repeatable quests, a choice of rewards, a gold cost and PvP quests always wait for you, and grey quests aren't auto-accepted. They do nothing in the Gamepad UI.\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffGamepad mode prompt|r, on by default. Turn it off to stop FlareUI asking about Blizzard's Gamepad UI when you press a controller button, handy for ConsolePort. |cffffd100/fui pad|r still switches.\n• Resource Bars: |cffffffffOnly When In Use|r in the Show dropdown of the swing timers. A bar appears when its weapon swings, so there's no off-hand or ranged bar unless you're using one.\n• Brazilian Portuguese translation, thanks to paulovnas.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Swing timers now default to Only When In Use. If yours were on Combat, they probably changed too: pick Combat in each bar's Show dropdown in Edit Mode to go back.\n• Chat: an unread whisper tab now shows in your whisper colour instead of red, and Battle.net whispers in their own colour.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: closing a tab scrolls the tabs back to the first one.\n• Minimap: the day/night button goes back to its corner if something moves it. Players with EnhanceQoL reported it stuck over the calendar and clock.\n• Move Any Frame: a group finder page still detached from its window now snaps back when it opens, even with Move Any Frame off." },
